+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+Each bug is a one-line divergence from the README, found in `src/catalog.ts` (`find` trims but does not upper-case, while products are stored under canonical SKUs), `src/shipping.ts` (`shippingCost` uses `>` against the threshold) and `src/tax.ts` (`lineVat` uses `Math.floor`). See proposal.md.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** make the three behaviours match the README with minimal edits, reusing existing helpers.
+
+**Non-Goals:** no refactor, no change to other rules or to the public API.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- `Catalog.find` uses the existing `canonicalSku`, so `get`, `getForSale`, `reprice` and `deactivate` all benefit from one fix. Alternative: canonicalise in the order code only; rejected because it leaves other entry points broken.
+- `shippingCost` uses `>=` against `FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS` (5000).
+- `lineVat` uses `percentOf` from `src/money.ts`, which does integer half-up division; no floating point is introduced.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Stored VAT of already-placed orders is not recomputed → out of scope; only new pricing changes.
