+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Three reports show the code disagreeing with the README business rules: a lower-case SKU (`lb-220`) is refused as an unknown product, an order whose goods come to exactly €50.00 is charged shipping, and a line's VAT can be one cent low (€1.99 at 22% shows €0.43, should be €0.44).
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Catalogue lookups canonicalise the SKU (trim, upper case) so `lb-220`, ` LB-220 ` and `LB-220` are the same product when ordering.
+- Shipping is free when the goods (after every discount, before VAT) are €50.00 **or more**; today exactly €50.00 still pays.
+- Line VAT is rounded half up to the cent, in integer cents, instead of rounded down.
+
+README rules affected: "Products" (SKUs case-insensitive and trimmed), "Shipping" (free from €50.00), "VAT" (half-up rounding per line). None of them is altered: the code is brought in line, so no README edit is needed.
+
+Out of scope: coupon-code handling, volume discounts, shipping VAT, invoices, the weight bands, and any other rule.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `product-catalog`: SKU identity (case-insensitive, trimmed, shown upper case) when products are looked up.
+- `shipping`: Shipping cost by weight band and the free-shipping threshold.
+- `vat`: Per-line VAT rounding half up to the cent.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+Code: `src/catalog.ts` (`find`), `src/shipping.ts` (`shippingCost`), `src/tax.ts` (`lineVat`). Tests in `test/*.test.ts`. No API, dependency or README change.
