+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+
+Defines how VAT on order lines is computed and rounded.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Line VAT rounds half up to the cent
+VAT SHALL be computed per line on the line's net amount after every discount, at the rate of its VAT class (standard 22%, reduced 10%, super-reduced 4%, exempt 0%), in integer cents, rounded half up on each line.
+
+#### Scenario: Below half a cent rounds down
+- **WHEN** a standard-rate line has net 100 cents
+- **THEN** its VAT is 22 cents
+
+#### Scenario: Above half a cent rounds up
+- **WHEN** a standard-rate line has net 199 cents (43.78 cents of VAT before rounding)
+- **THEN** its VAT is 44 cents
+
+#### Scenario: Exactly half a cent rounds up
+- **WHEN** a reduced-rate (10%) line has net 205 cents (20.5 cents)
+- **THEN** its VAT is 21 cents
